  "title": "dfilter: resolve unparsed for each node in a set",
  "description": "In check_relation_in, make sure we resolve each unparsed node\nin the set before calling check relation on the outer LHS field.\nCall it with strict == false because literals are allowed.\n\nThe latter changes the test a bit because \"22-33-\" now gets a\nsomewhat more useful error message about being a possible but\ntruncated Ethernet address instead of \"not a field\" in a case\nwhere it could be a literal Ethernet address.\n\nFix #20183",
